- ## Scope
- Updated three remote macOS OpenClaw installs to `2026.5.12-beta.4` (`d124625`) using:
- ```sh
- openclaw update --channel beta --tag 2026.5.12-beta.4 --yes --timeout 1800
- ```
- ```
- ```
- ```
- Host identifiers, usernames, IPs, local personal paths, channel tokens, account IDs, session IDs, and private prompt or workspace content are intentionally omitted or generalized.
- ## Starting Versions
- - Host A: `2026.5.12-beta.3`
- - Host B: `2026.5.10-beta.3`
- - Host C: `2026.5.12-beta.2`
- All three were already configured for the `beta` update channel and reported `2026.5.12-beta.4` available before update.
- ## Update Result
- All three installs completed the package update successfully:
- - `Root: /opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw`
- - `After: 2026.5.12-beta.4`
- - Package manager/install mode reported as `pnpm`
- - Managed LaunchAgent was stopped before package update
- - Gateway ended up running after update
- Post-update verification on all three:
- - `openclaw --version`: `OpenClaw 2026.5.12-beta.4 (d124625)`
- - `openclaw update status`: `up to date · npm beta 2026.5.12-beta.4`
- - `openclaw gateway status --deep`: LaunchAgent loaded, gateway running, connectivity probe OK, CLI version and gateway version both `2026.5.12-beta.4`
- - `openclaw plugins doctor`: `No plugin issues detected`, with a deprecation warning: `plugin runtime config.loadConfig() is deprecated (runtime-config-load-write); use config.current().`
- - Channel checks were reachable after update
- - Direct non-delivered agent checks succeeded on all three with `openai/gpt-5.5`, `agentHarnessId: codex`, and `fallbackUsed: false`
- ## Maintainer-Facing Bugs/Issues
- ### 1. Update restart phase emits stale CLI/config-version mismatch on all three npm installs
- After the package update and plugin update completed, all three hosts emitted the same restart-time warning:
- ```text
- ```text
- ```text
- Restarting service...
- Your OpenClaw config was written by version 2026.5.12-beta.4, but this command is running <previous-version>.
- Check: `openclaw --version`, `which openclaw`, and `openclaw gateway status --deep`.
- If unexpected, update PATH so `openclaw` points to the version you want, or reinstall the Gateway service from that same OpenClaw install.
- Gateway already reports the updated version after service refresh; skipped redundant restart.
- The `<previous-version>` value matched each host's pre-update CLI (`2026.5.12-beta.3`, `2026.5.10-beta.3`, and `2026.5.12-beta.2` respectively).
- Observed outcome was healthy, but the warning is confusing and looks like a real version-skew failure during a successful update. It also suggests the post-install restart logic is still executing in the pre-update process after config has been written by the new version.
- Expected behavior: for package-manager updates, post-install restart/verification should either re-exec through the updated entrypoint or report this as an expected updater self-staleness case without alarming operators. If an older process intentionally remains in charge of the restart, the message should distinguish that known case from an actual operator PATH/service mismatch.
- Likely source area in the local checkout:
- - `src/cli/update-cli/update-command.ts`
- - `src/cli/update-cli.test.ts`
- - related future-config guard tests under `src/cli/daemon-cli/`
- ### 2. `plugins doctor` reports a deprecated runtime config API even while saying no plugin issues
- On all three hosts, `openclaw plugins doctor` printed:
- plugin runtime config.loadConfig() is deprecated (runtime-config-load-write); use config.current().
- No plugin issues detected.
- This may be expected while third-party plugins migrate, but as operator output it is awkward: the command says no plugin issues while also surfacing a runtime deprecation. It is not clear which plugin caused it or whether action is required.
- Expected behavior: either attribute the deprecation to a plugin ID/path or treat it as a doctor finding with actionable output. If the deprecation is purely internal/noise, suppress it from `plugins doctor` success output.
- Relevant source area:
- Relevant source area:
- - `src/plugins/runtime/runtime-config.ts`
- - plugin implementations still using `runtime.config.loadConfig()`
- ### 3. External plugin beta fallback is not summarized as drift after update
- On one host, a configured external plugin had no beta npm release:
- Plugin "lossless-claw" has no beta npm release for @martian-engineering/lossless-claw@beta; using @martian-engineering/lossless-claw@latest instead. Core update can still complete.
- This is probably a reasonable fallback, but the end state leaves the host on a beta OpenClaw core with at least one external plugin intentionally pinned to `latest`. The update result says OK, and later security output reports unpinned npm specs, but there is no compact update-summary section calling out the mixed-channel plugin state.
- Expected behavior: the final update summary should include a clear "plugin channel fallback/mixed channel" note when `@beta` falls back to `@latest`, so operators do not have to spot it in the middle of install logs.
- - `src/plugins/update.ts`
- - `src/plugins/plugin-peer-link.ts`
- ## Additional Operator Notes
- These were not treated as beta-update regressions:
- - One host had a pre-update stalled agent run causing gateway timeout during baseline doctor. Restart during update cleared gateway reachability; post-update gateway status was OK.
- - One host had a pre-existing gateway token source conflict (`OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN` vs `gateway.auth.token`) that remained after update.
- - Task audits continued to show stale/lost/delivery warnings that predated the update.
- - One direct agent check used the phrase "smoke test"; that triggered a local `smoke-test` skill and caused tool calls plus a memory write before returning `OK`. This looks like a skill-trigger/operator-footgun observation, not evidence that the beta update itself failed.
- ## PR Candidates For A Non-Engineer Using Codex/Claude
- 1. Update the restart-phase message for package updates so the known stale parent updater process is not reported like an unexpected PATH/config mismatch. Start in `src/cli/update-cli/update-command.ts` and add/adjust a focused test in `src/cli/update-cli.test.ts`.
- 2. Improve plugin update summary output when a channel-specific plugin version falls back to `@latest`. Start in `src/plugins/update.ts`; likely mostly formatting and tests.
- 3. Attribute or suppress the `runtime.config.loadConfig()` deprecation warning in `plugins doctor` success output. Start in `src/plugins/runtime/runtime-config.ts` and search for remaining plugin `loadConfig()` callers.

